    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1054">

                <pb facs="1327" n="1317" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg1317"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.48/6–1847: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-06-18T15:00:00+09:00">June 18, 1947—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 18—4:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1324. Embassy has now received from Foreign Office detailed requests for
                    post-UNRRA relief along lines described Embassy’s telegram <pb facs="1328"
                        n="1318" xml:id="pg1318"/> 1274 [<hi rendition="#italic">1275</hi>], June
                    12, 11 a.m., together with request third meeting Sino–U. S. working group be
                    held June 20 to discuss them.</p>
                <p>Embassy expressed unwillingness to discuss request (copies being airmailed<anchor
                        n="39" xml:id="d1054-f1"/>) without opportunity to inspect them closely and
                    agreed meeting be held June 23. Accordingly Embassy should receive Department’s
                    instructions, especially with reference Embassy’s telegram 1184, May 31, 1 p.m.;
                    Consulate General’s telegram Shanghai 1325, June 1, 1 p.m.;<anchor n="40"
                        xml:id="d1054-f2"/> Embassy’s telegram 1275, June 12, 11 a.m., and Embassy’s
                    telegram 1276, June 12, noon, to be despatched by urgent telegram from
                    Washington not later than Friday<anchor n="41" xml:id="d1054-f3"/> p.m.
                    Washington time.</p>
                <p>Highly desirable that clear cut statements of policy and plan for future
                    operation of post-UNRRA relief be given Chinese now.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Shanghai 548.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
